C("Classic: a license seat pool",
  "Write LicensePool with `assign(user)` (return True and record the user if a seat is free, else False) and `release(user)`. A user who already has a seat should get True without using another. It should print: True, True, False, True",
  "class LicensePool:\n    def __init__(self, seats):\n        self.seats = seats\n        self.users = set()\n\n    # TODO: assign(self, user) and release(self, user)\n\npool = LicensePool(2)\nprint(pool.assign('ada'))\nprint(pool.assign('bob'))\nprint(pool.assign('cy'))\npool.release('ada')\nprint(pool.assign('cy'))",
  "class LicensePool:\n    def __init__(self, seats):\n        self.seats = seats\n        self.users = set()\n\n    def assign(self, user):\n        if user in self.users:\n            return True\n        if len(self.users) >= self.seats:\n            return False\n        self.users.add(user)\n        return True\n\n    def release(self, user):\n        self.users.discard(user)\n\npool = LicensePool(2)\nprint(pool.assign('ada'))\nprint(pool.assign('bob'))\nprint(pool.assign('cy'))\npool.release('ada')\nprint(pool.assign('cy'))",
  "def assign(self, user):\n    if user in self.users:\n        return True\n    if len(self.users) >= self.seats:\n        return False\n    self.users.add(user)\n    return True\n\ndef release(self, user):\n    self.users.discard(user)",
  [("A set holds who has a seat", "`user in self.users` is an O(1) check, and the set can't hold the same user twice. `len(self.users)` is how many seats are taken.",
    "taken = {'ada'}\nprint('ada' in taken, len(taken))"),
   ("Order the checks", "First: already has a seat, return True. Then: full, return False. Otherwise add and return True. `discard` removes a user without failing if they're absent.",
    "s = {'a', 'b'}\ns.discard('a')\ns.discard('z')\nprint(s)")]),
